/* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   THE THREAD'S CARD (dev-board/topic/thread-card.tsx). Beside "How it got
   here", a request's and a change's page draw the thread as one card: a
   kicker (the project, then "Request #N" or "Change #N"), the title, the
   words and whose they are, the picture, and a foot that says where it
   stands and holds the action. A step of the timeline opens its content
   over the card, as a layer that never changes the card's height.

   The pieces are rendered only under the standard look and the brand look
   (the frame's looks keep their own page), so nothing here needs a look in
   its selector: every rule hangs off a class those pages alone render.
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */
/* THE ⋯ ON THE CARD'S FIRST LINE (17 Nov 2026). The sheet's header row
   held only the topic's name and ⋯ under the card look: a band about 70px
   tall above every card, on a phone too. The header keeps its markup (the
   ⋯ and what selects on it), takes no height, and its ⋯ sits over the end
   of the card's kicker line; the topic is said in the kicker instead. */
.dev-request:has(.dev-thread-card) .dev-request-bar { height: 0; position: relative; z-index: 5; box-shadow: none; }
.dev-request:has(.dev-thread-card) .dev-request-bar .messages-thread-header { padding: 6px 10px 0; pointer-events: none; }
.dev-request:has(.dev-thread-card) .dev-request-bar .messages-thread-action { pointer-events: auto; }
.dev-request:has(.dev-thread-card) .dev-request-bar :is([data-request-category], [data-change-category]) {
  position: absolute; width: 1px; height: 1px; overflow: hidden; clip-path: inset(50%); white-space: nowrap;
}
.dev-request:has(.dev-request-bar [data-card-menu]) .dev-thread-kicker { padding-inline-end: 44px; }
/* THE REPLY BOX FOLLOWS THE REPLIES (17 Nov 2026). The scroller filled the
   sheet, so the box was pinned to the bottom of the window however short
   the thread: far under a card with two replies. The scroller is now only
   as tall as what it holds, so the box sits right under the replies, and
   it is pinned again (the scroller shrinks and scrolls) once the thread is
   taller than the window. */
.dev-request:has(.dev-thread-card) .dev-request-scroll { flex-grow: 0; }
/* …BUT A PRIVATE THREAD KEEPS ITS BOX AT THE FOOT (24 Nov 2026). A private
   thread with Homeroom bot is a chat, and a chat keeps its reply box at the
   bottom of the column: with a message or two the box stood in the middle
   of the screen under a short card, the rest of the column bare. There the
   scroller fills the sheet again, as a column of the cards, and the
   replies' card fills it down to the reply box: its foot is the 12px the
   spacer after it leaves over the box (THE FOOT IS A SPACER, below), as a
   long thread's is. The messages start at the card's top, and one more is
   added under the last without the card changing height. Nothing in the
   column shrinks: a thread taller than the column scrolls as it did, and
   the spacer, an empty item, would otherwise be the first thing a column
   squeezed. Wherever the page is drawn: beside the lists, beside a
   preview, and in a phone's drawer. Request and change pages keep the box
   under their replies (the rule above). */
#ai-screen .dev-private-thread .dev-request-scroll {
  flex-grow: 1;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
}
#ai-screen .dev-private-thread .dev-request-scroll > *,
#ai-screen .dev-private-thread .dev-request-scroll::after { flex-shrink: 0; }
#ai-screen .dev-private-thread .dev-request-scroll > [data-thread-page-replies] { flex-grow: 1; }
/* The author row gives way to the kicker; the timeline says who and when. */
.dev-thread-card { position: relative; --foot-x: 16px; --foot-b: 16px; }
/* The card's own gutters, so the foot's band can reach its edges exactly. */
.dev-request-root.dev-thread-card { padding: 4px var(--foot-x) var(--foot-b); }
@media (min-width: 1180px) { .dev-thread-card { --foot-x: 20px; --foot-b: 18px; } }
.dev-thread-card > :first-child:not(.min-w-0) { display: none; }
.dev-thread-card .messages-message-head { display: none; }
.dev-thread-kicker { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; margin: 0 0 6px; font-size: 13px; line-height: 20px; font-weight: 500; color: var(--text-secondary); overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
.dev-thread-kicker-tile { flex: none; width: 20px; height: 20px; border-radius: 6px; font-size: 11px; overflow: hidden; display: grid; place-items: center; line-height: 1; }
/* #7170: the project's emoji or letter sits in the middle of the tile at the
   tile's own size, as the Workshop's other tiles do. The emoji arrives as a
   30px span; inherit makes it the tile's font size. A picture still fills the
   tile, and .app-icon-wait is positioned, so it is not a grid item. */
.app-icon-tile:is(.dev-thread-bar-tile, .dev-thread-kicker-tile) > span:not(.app-icon-wait) { font-size: inherit; line-height: 1; }
/* The sheet's header keeps the category and ⋯; the card says the rest. */
.dev-request:has(.dev-thread-card) #gc-thread-bar :is(.messages-thread-kicker, .messages-thread-name, [data-request-status], [data-change-status]) { display: none; }
.dev-thread-card .dev-request-title { font-size: 22px; line-height: 28px; letter-spacing: -0.01em; text-wrap: balance; }
/* The words are the card's own, not a quote of somebody. */
.dev-thread-card .dev-request-ask { margin-top: 6px; padding-inline: 0; border-inline-start: 0; }
.dev-thread-card .dev-request-ask-text { font-size: 15.5px; line-height: 24px; max-width: 70ch; }
.dev-thread-by { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px; margin: 6px 0 0; font-size: 12.5px; line-height: 18px; color: var(--text-muted); }
.dev-thread-by-glyph { flex: none; width: 14px; height: 14px; }

/* The foot: where it stands, once, and the action. */
/* A band across the card: its line and its ground reach the card's edges,
   and where the foot ends the card (thread-card.tsx marks it) the band runs
   to the card's own rounded end. */
.dev-thread-foot {
  display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 10px 14px;
  margin: 16px calc(-1 * var(--foot-x)) 0; padding: 14px var(--foot-x);
  border-top: 1px solid var(--app-sheet-line);
  background: var(--thread-foot, transparent);
}
.dev-thread-foot[data-thread-foot-end] {
  margin-bottom: calc(-1 * var(--foot-b)); padding-bottom: 16px;
  border-radius: 0 0 var(--thread-card-r, 0px) var(--thread-card-r, 0px);
}
.dev-thread-foot-st { flex: 1 1 180px; min-width: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 2px; }
.dev-thread-foot-head { font-size: 17px; line-height: 22px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--text-primary); overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
.dev-thread-foot[data-thread-foot-tone="bad"] .dev-thread-foot-head { color: var(--state-blocked); }
.dev-thread-foot[data-thread-foot-tone="ok"] .dev-thread-foot-head { color: var(--state-ok); }
.dev-thread-foot[data-thread-foot-tone="muted"] .dev-thread-foot-head { color: var(--text-secondary); }
.dev-thread-foot-sub { font-size: 13px; line-height: 18px; color: var(--text-secondary); overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
.dev-thread-foot-bar { display: block; height: 4px; max-width: 280px; margin-top: 6px; border-radius: 2px; background: var(--messages-hair); overflow: hidden; }
.dev-thread-foot-bar > i { display: block; height: 100%; border-radius: 2px; background: var(--lit-ink); }
.dev-thread-foot-acts { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 8px; }
/* The foot's actions are full pills: the one to press, and the quieter ones
   beside it. The vote's caret is put away: one Vote, and the question after. */
.dev-thread-foot-acts :is(button, a):not(.dev-change-gate-link) {
  height: 40px; min-height: 40px; padding-block: 0; padding-inline: 18px; border-radius: 999px;
  font-size: 15px; font-weight: 650; line-height: 1;
}
.dev-thread-foot-acts .dev-vote-caret { display: none; }
.dev-thread-foot-extra { flex-basis: 100%; min-width: 0; }
.dev-thread-foot-ask { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 8px 10px; }
.dev-thread-foot-q { flex-basis: 100%; margin: 0; font-size: 14.5px; line-height: 20px; font-weight: 650; color: var(--text-primary); }
.dev-thread-foot-also { margin: 0; font-size: 13px; line-height: 19px; color: var(--text-secondary); overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
.dev-thread-foot-also[data-thread-foot-also="bad"] > span { color: var(--state-blocked); }
@media (max-width: 520px) {
  .dev-thread-foot-acts { flex-basis: 100%; }
  /* On a phone the one to press takes the row it is on. */
  .dev-thread-foot-acts > :is(.dev-vote-btn, .dev-request-primary, :has(> .dev-vote-btn)):last-child { flex: 1 1 auto; }
  .dev-thread-foot-acts > :has(> .dev-vote-btn):last-child > .dev-vote-btn { width: 100%; }
  /* …and the others share it, so none is a small pill beside empty space. */
  .dev-thread-foot-acts > :is(button, a), .dev-thread-foot-acts > [data-thread-foot-next] > :is(button, a) { flex: 1 1 auto; justify-content: center; }
  .dev-thread-foot-acts > :has(> .dev-vote-btn) { flex: 1 1 auto; }
  .dev-thread-foot-acts > :has(> .dev-vote-btn) > .dev-vote-btn { width: 100%; }
}


/* Where the picture will be, before there is one. Every well a picture
   stands in reads --thread-well first: the standard look's thread page sets
   it to the ground behind its cards (see "WHERE THE PICTURE GOES" above the
   generated block); every other look leaves it unset. */
.dev-thread-wait,
.dev-thread-card .dev-change-shots-plain {
  margin-top: 14px; min-height: 132px; padding: 20px;
  display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; justify-content: center; gap: 6px;
  border-radius: 16px; text-align: center;
  background: var(--thread-well, var(--messages-surface-2)); box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--app-sheet-line);
  color: var(--text-secondary);
}
/* The caption under the tiles is one quiet line a change, not a heading:
   the bold claim is for the expanded view. */
.dev-thread-tiles-legend .shots-change strong { font-size: 13.5px; line-height: 19px; font-weight: 400; color: var(--text-secondary); }
.dev-thread-tiles-legend .shots-change-n { width: 18px; height: 18px; font-size: 11px; }
/* The one before & after viewer (review-flow/shots-viewer.tsx): the Needs
   you page's slider (.rf-compare), in the card's own colours. No outline and
   no tint: the seam is what tells the two sides apart. Expand opens the same
   viewer, larger, in the detail column. */
.dev-thread-picture { margin-top: 14px; overflow: visible; background: none; }
.dev-thread-compare {
  --rf-black: var(--text-primary); --rf-cream: var(--bg-primary); --rf-line: var(--app-sheet-line);
  position: relative; min-height: 120px; border-radius: 16px; overflow: hidden; isolation: isolate;
  background: var(--thread-well, var(--messages-surface-2));
}
.dev-thread-compare::after { content: ''; position: absolute; inset: 0; z-index: 4; border-radius: inherit; box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--app-sheet-line); pointer-events: none; }
.dev-thread-compare-expand {
  position: absolute; z-index: 5; inset-inline-end: 12px; bottom: 12px; width: 40px; height: 40px; padding: 0;
  display: grid; place-items: center; border: 1.5px solid var(--rf-black); border-radius: 999px;
  background: var(--rf-cream); color: var(--rf-black); cursor: pointer;
}
.dev-thread-compare-expand:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--accent); outline-offset: 3px; }
/* A run that took dark shots too: the other mode, at the picture's other foot. */
.dev-thread-compare-theme {
  position: absolute; z-index: 5; inset-inline-start: 12px; bottom: 12px; width: 40px; height: 40px; padding: 0;
  display: grid; place-items: center; border: 1.5px solid var(--rf-black); border-radius: 999px;
  background: var(--rf-cream); color: var(--rf-black); cursor: pointer;
}
.dev-thread-compare-theme:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--accent); outline-offset: 3px; }
/* Under the picture: the changes it shows, numbered in the quiet ink of the
   list below (no side owns a number), the changes no screen shows, what was
   noticed besides, and each motion change's two clips. */
.shots-one .shots-change-n { background: #3f3f46; }
.dark .shots-one .shots-change-n { color: #18181b; background: #d4d4d8; }
.shots-one .shots-change:hover { background: none; }
.shots-one > .shots-claims, .shots-one > .shots-noticed { margin-top: 12px; padding: 0 2px; }
.shots-one .shots-view-meta { margin-top: 8px; }
.shots-after-only { margin: 0 0 6px; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 650; color: var(--text-primary); }
.shots-missing { margin: 0; padding: 12px 14px; font-size: 13px; color: var(--state-err-ink, #b91c1c); }
.shots-clips { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: stretch; gap: 8px; margin-top: 8px; }
.shots-clip { flex: 1 1 200px; min-width: 0; margin: 0; }
.shots-clip-caption { margin-bottom: 4px; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .04em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--text-muted); }
.shots-clip-video { display: block; width: 100%; max-height: 360px; border-radius: 8px; background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35); }
.shots-clip-paired .shots-clip-video { margin-top: 6px; }
.shots-clip-none { display: grid; place-items: center; height: 120px; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px dashed var(--app-sheet-line); font-size: 12px; color: var(--text-muted); }
/* #7180: the row wraps, so the caption is never squeezed to a few letters by
   a row of six tiles. The room that matters is the card's, not the viewport's:
   a desktop side panel is about 540px wide, so the 520px media query below
   never applied there. The caption asks for 12rem of its own; less than that
   left beside the tiles and it takes the next line, at the row's full width. */
.dev-thread-tiles { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; margin-top: 10px; padding: 0 2px 4px; }
.dev-thread-tile { flex: none; width: 64px; height: 48px; border-radius: 10px; overflow: hidden; background: var(--thread-well, var(--messages-surface-2)); box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--app-sheet-line); }
.dev-thread-tile > img { display: block; width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; object-position: top; }
/* The ring's gap falls back to the page's ground where the viewer is drawn
   outside a thread (the detail column, the preview's tab, the admin gallery). */
.dev-thread-tile[aria-pressed="true"] { box-shadow: 0 0 0 2px var(--messages-surface, var(--bg-primary, #fff)), 0 0 0 4px var(--text-primary); }
.dev-thread-tiles-cap { flex: 1 1 12rem; min-width: min(12rem, 100%); }
.dev-thread-tiles-count { margin: 0 0 2px; font-size: 13px; line-height: 18px; font-weight: 650; color: var(--text-primary); }
.dev-thread-tiles-legend { display: block; }
@media (max-width: 520px) { .dev-thread-tiles { flex-wrap: wrap; } .dev-thread-tiles-cap { flex-basis: 100%; } }
/* #6814: "What it touches" takes the empty box's place on a change's page,
   so it keeps the box's distance from the summary above it. */
.dev-thread-card .dev-ws-touches { margin-top: 14px; }
.dev-thread-wait > b { font-size: 14.5px; line-height: 20px; font-weight: 650; color: var(--text-primary); }
.dev-thread-wait > span { max-width: 46ch; font-size: 13.5px; line-height: 20px; }

/* A step's content, over the card. */
.dev-step-layer { position: absolute; inset: 0; z-index: 6; }
.dev-step-scrim { position: absolute; inset: -6px; top: var(--step-floor, -6px); border-radius: 14px; background: var(--messages-surface); opacity: 0.78; cursor: default; }
.dev-step-sheet {
  position: absolute; inset-inline: 0; top: 8px;
  overflow: auto; overscroll-behavior: contain;
  padding: 0 16px 16px; border-radius: 16px;
  background: var(--messages-surface-2);
  box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--app-sheet-line), 0 14px 36px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.2);
  animation: dev-step-rise 0.16s ease-out;
}
@keyframes dev-step-rise { from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(6px); } to { opacity: 1; transform: none; } }
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { .dev-step-sheet { animation: none; } }
:where(html[data-motion="reduce"]) .dev-step-sheet { animation: none; }
.dev-step-head {
  position: sticky; top: 0; z-index: 2;
  display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px;
  margin: 0 -16px; padding: 12px 16px 8px;
  background: var(--messages-surface-2); box-shadow: 0 1px 0 var(--app-sheet-line);
  border-radius: 16px 16px 0 0;
}
.dev-step-title { display: block; font-size: 15px; line-height: 20px; font-weight: 650; color: var(--text-primary); }
.dev-step-sub { display: block; font-size: 13px; line-height: 18px; color: var(--text-secondary); }
.dev-step-when { font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--text-muted); white-space: nowrap; }
.dev-step-close {
  flex: none; width: 30px; height: 30px; border-radius: 50%;
  display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
  background: var(--messages-surface); box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--app-sheet-line);
  color: var(--text-primary);
}
.dev-step-body { padding-top: 12px; }
.dev-step-doc { font-size: 15px; line-height: 24px; color: var(--text-secondary); overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
.dev-step-doc .dev-issue-body { font-size: inherit; color: inherit; }
/* The plan reader's body inside the layer: the sheet already carries its inset. */
.dev-step-doc .gc-spec-panel-body { padding: 0; }
.dev-step-plain { margin: 0; font-size: 14px; line-height: 20px; color: var(--text-secondary); }
.dev-step-who { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; margin-bottom: 8px; font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-secondary); }
.dev-step-who > b { font-weight: 650; color: var(--text-primary); }
@media (max-width: 520px) { .dev-step-when { display: none; } .dev-step-sheet { padding-inline: 12px; } .dev-step-head { margin-inline: -12px; padding-inline: 12px; } }

/* One step, one thing: the Tested step's layer shows the tests, the vote's
   step its votes (change-head.tsx ChangeGates). */
/* The tests as counts and rows (change-head.tsx ChecksSummary); the Testing
   card under it is put away while they are drawn. */
[data-gates-show="checks"]:has(> [data-checks-summary]) .dev-change-pair [data-change-gate="testing"] { display: none; }
.dev-thread-facts { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 6px; margin: 10px 0 0; }
.dev-thread-fact {
  display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px; min-height: 28px; padding: 3px 10px; border-radius: 999px;
  background: var(--thread-fact, var(--messages-surface)); box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--app-sheet-line);
  font-size: 13px; line-height: 18px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-secondary);
}
.dev-thread-fact[data-tone="bad"] { background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--state-blocked) 12%, transparent); box-shadow: none; color: var(--state-blocked); }
.dev-thread-fact[data-tone="ok"] { background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--state-ok) 14%, transparent); box-shadow: none; color: var(--state-ok); }
.dev-checks-sum > .dev-thread-facts { margin-top: 0; }
.dev-checks-why { margin: 10px 0 0; font-size: 13.5px; line-height: 20px; color: var(--text-secondary); overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
.dev-checks-rows { list-style: none; margin: 10px 0 0; padding: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px; }
.dev-checks-row {
  display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 2px; padding: 10px 12px; border-radius: 12px;
  background: var(--thread-fact, var(--messages-surface)); box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--app-sheet-line);
  font-size: 13px; line-height: 19px; color: var(--text-secondary); overflow-wrap: anywhere;
}
.dev-checks-row > b { display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 8px; font-size: 14px; line-height: 20px; font-weight: 650; color: var(--text-primary); }
.dev-checks-row > b > svg { margin-top: 3px; color: var(--state-blocked); }
.dev-checks-row[data-checks-row="advisory"] > b > svg { color: var(--text-muted); }
.dev-checks-acts { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; margin-top: 12px; }
.dev-checks-acts:empty { display: none; }
[data-gates-show="checks"] .dev-change-pair [data-change-gate="votes"],
[data-gates-show="votes"] .dev-change-pair :is([data-change-gate="testing"], [data-change-gate="merge"]) { display: none; }

/* A request with competing changes: a row each, its picture first, then its
   letter and name, what its tests say and its yes votes, and Look, which
   opens the change over the card. */
.dev-thread-opts { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px; margin-top: 14px; }
.dev-thread-opt {
  display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 14px; width: 100%; padding: 10px; border-radius: 16px; text-align: start;
  background: var(--thread-opt, var(--messages-surface)); box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--app-sheet-line);
}
@media (hover: hover) { .dev-thread-opt:hover { box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--text-muted); } }
.dev-thread-opt-pic {
  flex: none; width: 132px; height: 84px; border-radius: 10px; overflow: hidden;
  display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
  background: var(--messages-surface-2); box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--app-sheet-line);
  font-size: 22px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--text-muted);
}
.dev-thread-opt-pic > img { display: block; width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; object-position: top; }
.dev-thread-opt-main { flex: 1 1 auto; min-width: 0; }
.dev-thread-opt-name { display: block; font-size: 15.5px; line-height: 21px; font-weight: 650; color: var(--text-primary); overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
.dev-thread-opt-line { display: block; margin-top: 2px; font-size: 13px; line-height: 18px; color: var(--text-secondary); overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
.dev-thread-opt-line [data-opt-tests="bad"] { color: var(--state-blocked); font-weight: 600; }
.dev-thread-opt-look { flex: none; display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 4px; padding-inline: 4px 6px; font-size: 14.5px; font-weight: 650; color: var(--accent); white-space: nowrap; }
@media (max-width: 520px) { .dev-thread-opt-pic { width: 84px; height: 60px; font-size: 18px; } .dev-thread-opt { gap: 10px; } }
/* A change opened over the card from its row: the section its fold held. */
.dev-step-body > [data-thread-look] { padding-bottom: 4px; }

/* The timeline: a step with something to show is one press, the whole step. */
.dev-rail-step { display: block; padding: 0; }
.dev-rail-press { display: flex; gap: 12px; width: 100%; padding: 6px 6px 12px; border-radius: 12px; text-align: start; }
.dev-rail-step:last-child .dev-rail-press { padding-bottom: 6px; }
.dev-rail-desc, .dev-rail-note { display: block; }
@media (hover: hover) { button.dev-rail-press:hover { background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--rail-line) 55%, transparent); } }
/* The step the thread stands on is boxed, so the eye lands on it. */
.dev-rail-step[data-rail-now] .dev-rail-press { background: var(--rail-now-box, transparent); box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--rail-now-box-line, transparent); }
.dev-rail-step[data-rail-on] .dev-rail-press { background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--rail-line) 55%, transparent); box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--rail-line); }
@media (max-width: 1179.98px) {
  .dev-rail-step { padding: 0; }
  .dev-rail-press { padding: 4px 6px 6px; }
  .dev-rail-step[data-rail-now] { padding-top: 0; }
  .dev-rail-step[data-rail-now] .dev-rail-press { padding-top: 8px; }
}

/* ONE SCALE ON A PHONE'S THREAD PAGE (#7171). The three cards under the head
   (the change, "How it got here" and the replies) each had sizes of their
   own: 12.5, 13.5, 14.5, 15.5 and 17px, close enough together to read as a
   mistake. Under 768px they take the platform's scale instead: words at
   15px, times and second lines at 13px, the one small label at 12px, and the
   head's title as the page's only larger line at 18px. Written in rem, so
   Settings' Text size scales them, as it does the rest of the shell. Desktop
   widths, the side panel's sizes on a wide screen and the frame's own looks
   are untouched. */
@media (max-width: 767.98px) {
  /* The head's title is the one larger line; its tight state keeps its own. */
  html:root #dev-topic-thread .dev-request:has(.dev-thread-card):not([data-thread-head-tight]) :is(#gc-thread-bar, .dev-request-bar) .dev-thread-bar-text > .messages-thread-name { font-size: 1.125rem; line-height: 1.5rem; }
  /* The card. */
  html:root #dev-topic-thread .dev-thread-card .dev-request-title { font-size: 1.125rem; line-height: 1.5rem; }
  html:root #dev-topic-thread .dev-thread-card .dev-request-ask-text { font-size: 0.9375rem; line-height: 1.375rem; }
  html:root #dev-topic-thread .dev-thread-by { font-size: 0.8125rem; }
  /* Its foot: the headline stays bold, at the words' size. */
  html:root #dev-topic-thread .dev-thread-foot-head { font-size: 0.9375rem; line-height: 1.25rem; }
  html:root #dev-topic-thread .dev-thread-foot-q { font-size: 0.9375rem; }
  html:root #dev-topic-thread .dev-thread-wait > b { font-size: 0.9375rem; }
  html:root #dev-topic-thread .dev-thread-wait > span { font-size: 0.8125rem; }
  html:root #dev-topic-thread :is(.dev-checks-why, .dev-thread-tiles-said, .dev-thread-tiles-legend .shots-change strong) { font-size: 0.8125rem; }
  html:root #dev-topic-thread :is(.dev-thread-opt-name, .dev-thread-opt-look) { font-size: 0.9375rem; }
  /* "How it got here": one small label, its steps at the words' size. */
  html:root #dev-topic-thread .dev-rail-title { font-size: 0.75rem; }
  html:root #dev-topic-thread .dev-rail-time { font-size: 0.8125rem; }
  html:root #dev-topic-thread :is(.dev-rail-pile-more, .dev-rail-desc, .dev-rail-note) { font-size: 0.8125rem; }
  html:root #dev-topic-thread .dev-rail-name { font-size: 0.9375rem; }
}

/* ── THE FACES THE PAGES NAME: Geist for words (--wip-font, --site-sans),
   Geist Mono for counts, Source Serif 4 and Young Serif for the editorial
   and signed-out headings (--ed-serif, --site-serif). ── */
@font-face {
  font-family: 'Geist';
  /* Absolute: the build-scoped copy of this sheet (/b/<sha>/css/app.css)
     serves only .js and .css, so a relative url would 404 there. A face is
     downloaded only when a rule that names it draws text. The same holds
     for the faces below. */
  src: url('/fonts/geist/Geist-Variable.woff2') format('woff2');
  font-weight: 100 900;
  font-style: normal;
  font-display: swap;
}
@font-face {
  font-family: 'Geist Mono';
  src: url('/fonts/geist-mono/GeistMono-Variable.woff2') format('woff2');
  font-weight: 100 900;
  font-style: normal;
  font-display: swap;
}
@font-face {
  font-family: 'Source Serif 4';
  src: url('/fonts/source-serif-4/source-serif-4-latin-opsz-normal.woff2') format('woff2');
  font-weight: 200 900;
  font-style: normal;
  font-display: swap;
}
@font-face {
  font-family: 'Young Serif';
  src: url('/fonts/young-serif/young-serif-latin-400-normal.woff2') format('woff2');
  font-weight: 400;
  font-style: normal;
  font-display: swap;
}

/* ══ ONE LOOK (design review, 25 Nov 2026): "B + sticker accents" across every
   page, on a phone and on a desktop. Each area below keeps its own rules together; they come last so they
   settle what the earlier per-screen rules left different.
     Shared parts: the sticker edge (ink outline, hard 2px shadow) only on a
     page's main action and its menu chips; every other button flat; a row's
     label (Read, Vote, Reply) a flat tag, never a button; segmented controls
     an ink pill on a light track; the tab bar's sun pill slides; rows 16/14 on
     a phone and 15/13 from 768px; the cream wash behind cards on every tab. ══ */
/* ── ONE LOOK · SHARED PARTS ── */
/* The values every area below draws with, declared once, in light and in dark. */
html:root {
  --one-ink: #121a0e;              /* words */
  --one-ink-2: #5b5e55;            /* a row's second line, a time */
  --one-ink-3: #8d9087;            /* a placeholder, a chevron */
  --one-sun: #ffee6f;              /* the main action, and where you are */
  --one-sun-hover: #fff59f;        /* the main action under a pointer */
  --one-sun-pale: #fff4b3;         /* a lit row inside a page (Settings' open section) */
  --one-sky: #3c7bd8;              /* the bars */
  --one-sky-ink: #1f5fbf;          /* a secondary action's words */
  --one-sky-tint: #e8effa;         /* a secondary action's fill, a tag's fill */
  --one-sky-tint-hover: #dde7f7;   /* a secondary action under a pointer */
  --one-red: #b4321e;
  --one-red-tint: #fbe7e3;
  --one-red-tint-hover: #f8dcd6;
  --one-link-line: #3090e1;        /* the underline of a text action, and the keyboard's focus ring */
  --one-surface: #ffffff;          /* a card */
  --one-hair: rgb(18 26 14 / 0.08);   /* a card's one hairline */
  --one-line: rgb(18 26 14 / 0.10);   /* a separator between rows */
  --one-field-line: rgb(18 26 14 / 0.14); /* a search field's or a chip's hairline */
  --one-quiet: rgb(18 26 14 / 0.06);  /* a quiet fill: a segmented track, a quiet tag */
  --one-edge-line: var(--wip-btn-line, #121a0e);   /* a sticker's outline */
  --one-edge-shade: var(--one-edge-line);          /* the hard edge under it: the outline's ink in light, darker than the ground in dark */
  --one-edge-sun-line: #121a0e;                    /* the outline of a sticker filled with the sun */
  --one-edge: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--one-edge-line), 2px 2px 0 0 var(--one-edge-shade);       /* the sticker edge */
  --one-edge-sm: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--one-edge-line), 1.5px 1.5px 0 0 var(--one-edge-shade);
  --one-edge-sun: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--one-edge-sun-line), 2px 2px 0 0 var(--one-edge-shade); /* the main action's */
  --one-edge-sun-sm: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--one-edge-sun-line), 1.5px 1.5px 0 0 var(--one-edge-shade);
  --one-press: translate(2px, 2px);  /* a sticker pressed onto its edge */
  --one-flat-press: scale(0.97);     /* a flat button pressed: a little smaller, a touch darker */
  --one-flat-dim: brightness(0.95);
  --one-tag-strong-bg: #121a0e;      /* the tag that asks for you ("1 to vote") */
  --one-tag-strong-ink: #ffffff;
  --one-seg-track: var(--one-quiet);
  --one-seg-thumb: #121a0e;
  --one-seg-ink: var(--one-ink-2);
  --one-seg-on-ink: #ffffff;
  --one-bubble-in: #f6f2d8;          /* their words */
  --one-bubble-out: #e3eefc;         /* yours */
  --one-tile-y-bg: #fdf2c2; --one-tile-y-ink: #7a5c00;   /* Needs you */
  --one-tile-b-bg: #e2ecfb; --one-tile-b-ink: #2f6fd1;   /* Workshop */
  --one-tile-g-bg: #e1f1dd; --one-tile-g-ink: #2f7a3b;   /* a discussion, a step done */
  --one-points: #9a3412;             /* a challenge's points */
  --one-progress: #cfe0fa;           /* a challenge's progress fill */
  --one-back-bg: #ffffff;            /* the back disc on the phone's blue bar */
  --one-back-ink: #121a0e;
  --one-row-title: 600 1rem/1.3125rem var(--wip-font, inherit);      /* rows: 16 over 14 on a phone (rem, so Text size scales them) */
  --one-row-sub: 400 0.875rem/1.1875rem var(--wip-font, inherit);
  /* A part's size on a phone; the desktop's density below. */
  --one-btn-h: 44px; --one-btn-pad: 20px; --one-btn-size: 16px;
  --one-chip-h: 34px; --one-chip-size: 14px;
  --one-fab: 40px;
}
@media (min-width: 768px) {
  html:root {
    --one-row-title: 600 0.9375rem/1.25rem var(--wip-font, inherit); /* 15 over 13 from 768px */
    --one-row-sub: 400 0.8125rem/1.125rem var(--wip-font, inherit);
    --one-btn-h: 36px; --one-btn-pad: 16px; --one-btn-size: 15px;
    --one-chip-h: 30px; --one-chip-size: 13px;
    --one-fab: 36px;
  }
}
html:root.dark {
  --one-ink: #fffeea;
  --one-ink-2: #c9c8b4;
  --one-ink-3: #8f8f80;
  --one-sun-pale: rgb(255 238 111 / 0.16);
  --one-sky-ink: #a8c4ff;
  --one-sky-tint: rgb(122 165 255 / 0.18);
  --one-sky-tint-hover: rgb(122 165 255 / 0.26);
  --one-red: #ff9c8a;
  --one-red-tint: rgb(255 156 138 / 0.16);
  --one-red-tint-hover: rgb(255 156 138 / 0.24);
  --one-surface: var(--wip-card-bg, #171715);
  --one-hair: rgb(255 254 234 / 0.10);
  --one-line: rgb(255 254 234 / 0.12);
  --one-field-line: rgb(255 254 234 / 0.18);
  --one-quiet: rgb(255 254 234 / 0.08);
  /* S8: in dark the hard edge is darker than the ground (a pale one read as a second outline out of register), and a
     sun sticker's outline is the sun, as the BUTTONS block draws the main action. */
  --one-edge-shade: rgb(0 0 0 / 0.7);
  --one-edge-sun-line: #ffee6f;
  --one-flat-dim: brightness(1.15);
  --one-tag-strong-bg: #fffeea;
  --one-tag-strong-ink: #121a0e;
  --one-seg-thumb: #fffeea;
  --one-seg-on-ink: #121a0e;
  --one-bubble-in: var(--dc-raised, #2c2c2e);
  --one-bubble-out: rgb(122 165 255 / 0.20);
  --one-tile-y-bg: rgb(255 238 111 / 0.16); --one-tile-y-ink: #ffe680;
  --one-tile-b-bg: rgb(122 165 255 / 0.18); --one-tile-b-ink: #a8c4ff;
  --one-tile-g-bg: rgb(159 212 154 / 0.16); --one-tile-g-ink: #9fd49a;
  --one-points: #ffb38a;
  --one-progress: rgb(122 165 255 / 0.30);
  --one-back-bg: #fffeea;
}
/* THE SHARED PARTS, each drawn once. Markup keeps its own ids and classes (the declared checks select on them) and adds
   the part's class; an area's own rules below only place a part, never redraw it. */
/* The tag for where something stands (StateTag, frontend/@/components/ui/state-tag.tsx): one part in three states, on
   every screen that says how far along a change or a request is. Plain says where it stands: an outline in the quiet
   ink ("Live", "0 of 1 approval", "3 new"). Working is plain with the turning mark (checking, being built, going live).
   Needs is the strong pill, for what asks for you ("3 to vote", "Vote", "Read"). The row is what you tap, so a tag never
   looks pressable: flat, no edge, no hover. An area's rule may place a tag, never repaint it. */
html:root .one-tag { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 5px; flex: none; max-width: 100%; height: 24px; padding: 0 9px; border: 0; border-radius: 9999px; background: transparent; color: var(--one-ink-2); font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; line-height: 1; letter-spacing: 0; white-space: nowrap; box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--one-field-line); overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; }
html:root .one-tag.one-tag-strong { background: var(--one-tag-strong-bg); color: var(--one-tag-strong-ink); box-shadow: none; }
html:root .one-tag > .dc-status-spinner-arc { flex: none; width: 11px; height: 11px; margin: 0; vertical-align: 0; }
html:root .one-tag > svg { flex: none; width: 12px; height: 12px; }
html:root .one-tag > .one-tag-words { min-width: 0; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; }
/* A segmented control: the chosen option an ink pill with white words, the rest grey on a light track. With
   --one-seg-n (options) and --one-seg-i (the chosen one's index) set on it, the pill slides between them. */
html:root .one-seg { position: relative; display: inline-grid; grid-auto-flow: column; grid-auto-columns: 1fr; align-items: stretch; min-height: 34px; padding: 2px; border: 0; border-radius: 9999px; background: var(--one-seg-track); box-shadow: none; isolation: isolate; }
html:root .one-seg > :is(button, a, [role="tab"], [role="radio"]) { position: relative; z-index: 1; display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; min-height: 30px; padding: 0 14px; border: 0; border-radius: 9999px; background: transparent; box-shadow: none; color: var(--one-seg-ink); font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; line-height: 1; white-space: nowrap; transition: color .2s ease, background-color .2s ease; }
html:root .one-seg > :is([aria-pressed="true"], [aria-selected="true"], [aria-checked="true"], [aria-current="page"]) { background: var(--one-seg-thumb); color: var(--one-seg-on-ink); }
html:root .one-seg[style*="--one-seg-i"]::before { content: ""; position: absolute; z-index: 0; top: 2px; bottom: 2px; inset-inline-start: 2px; width: calc((100% - 4px) / var(--one-seg-n, 2)); border-radius: 9999px; background: var(--one-seg-thumb); transform: translateX(calc(var(--one-seg-i, 0) * 100% * var(--rtl-sign, 1))); transition: transform .38s cubic-bezier(.3, 1.3, .5, 1); }
html:root .one-seg[style*="--one-seg-i"] > :is([aria-pressed="true"], [aria-selected="true"], [aria-checked="true"], [aria-current="page"]) { background: transparent; }
/* A control the kit hides by its `hidden` class (the change preview's Preview | Before & after) stays hidden: the
   track's own display would otherwise outrank the utility. */
html:root .one-seg.hidden { display: none; }
html:root .one-seg > :is(button, a, [role="tab"], [role="radio"]):focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--one-link-line); outline-offset: 2px; }
/* A menu chip opens a choice that sets what you are working on (All projects, About, With): a white pill with the small
   sticker edge, its label's lead word in the quiet ink. */
html:root .one-chip { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 4px; flex: none; height: var(--one-chip-h); padding: 0 10px 0 13px; border: 0; border-radius: 9999px; background: var(--one-surface); box-shadow: var(--one-edge-sm); color: var(--one-ink); font-family: var(--wip-btn-font, inherit); font-size: var(--one-chip-size); font-weight: 600; line-height: 1; white-space: nowrap; }
html:root .one-chip .one-chip-lead { color: var(--one-ink-2); font-weight: 400; }
html:root .one-chip > svg { width: 15px; height: 15px; flex: none; }
html:root .one-chip:active:not(:disabled) { box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--one-edge-line); transform: var(--one-press); }
/* The page's main action as an icon (New chat's +, New message's +): the sun disc with the sticker edge. */
html:root .one-fab { display: inline-grid; place-items: center; flex: none; width: var(--one-fab); height: var(--one-fab); padding: 0; border: 0; border-radius: 9999px; background: var(--one-sun); box-shadow: var(--one-edge-sun); color: #121a0e; }
html:root .one-fab:active:not(:disabled) { box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--one-edge-sun-line); transform: var(--one-press); }
@media (hover: hover) { html:root .one-fab:hover:not(:disabled, [aria-disabled="true"]) { background: var(--one-sun-hover); } }
/* The main action's recipe (one-btn-1): the sun with the sticker edge, pressed onto it, 44px on a phone and 36px from
   768px. The Button primitive's `sun` variant writes it (frontend/@/components/ui/button.tsx); the class-matching layer
   in BUTTONS draws every other button, the flat secondary and destructive ones included. */
html:root .one-btn { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; gap: 6px; flex: none; height: var(--one-btn-h); padding: 0 var(--one-btn-pad); border: 0; border-radius: 9999px; font-family: var(--wip-btn-font, inherit); font-size: var(--one-btn-size); font-weight: 600; line-height: 1; letter-spacing: 0; white-space: nowrap; text-decoration: none; transition: transform .12s ease, filter .12s ease; }
html:root .one-btn > svg { width: 18px; height: 18px; flex: none; }
html:root .one-btn.one-btn-1 { background: var(--one-sun); color: #121a0e; box-shadow: var(--one-edge-sun); }
html:root .one-btn.one-btn-1:active:not(:disabled, [aria-disabled="true"]) { box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--one-edge-sun-line); transform: var(--one-press); }
@media (hover: hover) {
  html:root .one-btn.one-btn-1:hover:not(:disabled, [aria-disabled="true"]) { background: var(--one-sun-hover); }
}
html:root :is(.one-btn, .one-chip, .one-fab):focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--one-link-line); outline-offset: 2px; }
html:root :is(.one-btn, .one-chip, .one-fab):is(:disabled, [aria-disabled="true"]) { opacity: .45; box-shadow: none; transform: none; filter: none; cursor: not-allowed; }
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  html:root .one-seg[style*="--one-seg-i"]::before,
  html:root .one-seg > :is(button, a, [role="tab"], [role="radio"]),
  html:root .one-btn { transition: none; }
}
html:root:where([data-motion="reduce"]) .one-seg[style*="--one-seg-i"]::before,
html:root:where([data-motion="reduce"]) .one-seg > :is(button, a, [role="tab"], [role="radio"]),
html:root:where([data-motion="reduce"]) .one-btn { transition: none; }

/* THE SUN SLIDES, ON THE PHONE'S BAR AND IN THE SIDEBAR (design review, 25 Nov 2026). Where you are was the lit tab's
   (the lit row's) own sun fill, which jumped from one to the next; the sliding marker (tab-bar.tsx useTabMarker) had
   been hidden on the phone since #7041, because both were drawn and the marker showed as a pale ring round the
   yellow. Now the marker IS the sun and the lit tab or row has no fill of its own, only the lit row's dark ink and
   its counts (the ink pill with white figures, ringed in the sun). On the phone it takes the lit tab's own box
   (`--platform-tabs-marker-fit: tab`, tabBoxFor), so the tabs keep their spacing: sized to their labels, a step
   clear of each other and of the bar's edges. In the sidebar it takes the lit row's box and corner
   (`--platform-tabs-marker-fit: row`, railLitRow and railBoxFor), Settings, a community's place and its row included,
   and the rows give up their fill only once it is placed, so before it is measured they are lit as before. A change
   of tab or row slides it (MARKER_SLIDE, a transform-only FLIP); reduced motion lands it. The offsets it is placed at
   are the bar's own from its left, in either reading direction. Not the iPhone Duo's side strip, which keeps each
   tab's own fill and hides the marker. */
html:root:not([data-side-strip]) #platform-tabs .platform-tabs-marker { inset: 0 auto auto 0; background: var(--wip-nav-on-bg); box-shadow: none; }
@media (max-width: 767.98px) {
  html:root:not([data-side-strip]) #platform-tabs { --platform-tabs-marker-fit: tab; }
  html:root:not([data-side-strip]) #platform-tabs .platform-tabs-marker { border-radius: var(--wip-nav-row-radius); }
  html:root:not([data-side-strip]) #platform-tabs .platform-tab[aria-current="page"] { background: transparent; }
}
@media (min-width: 768px) {
  html:root:not([data-side-strip]) #platform-tabs { --platform-tabs-marker-fit: row; }
  html:root:not([data-side-strip]) #platform-tabs .platform-tabs-marker { display: block; }
  html:root:not([data-side-strip]) #platform-tabs:has(> .platform-tabs-marker[data-marker-at]) :is(.platform-tab, .platform-rail-settings, .platform-rail-community, .dev-ws-place, .platform-rail-sub)[aria-current="page"] { background: transparent; }
  /* On the way to a community's page its places are drawn a beat after its row lights, so the pill waits on the row
     (railLitRow); the row is drawn at rest, in white, so while no place under it is lit it takes the lit row's ink,
     and its pin with it, as a lit row's does. */
  html:root:not([data-side-strip]) #platform-tabs:has(> .platform-tabs-marker[data-marker-at]) .platform-rail-row:has(> .platform-rail-community[data-rail-open][aria-current="page"]):not(:has(+ .platform-rail-nest:not([data-nest="closing"]) :is(.dev-ws-place, .platform-rail-sub)[aria-current="page"])) > .platform-rail-community {
    color: var(--wip-nav-on-ink);
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  html:root:not([data-side-strip]) #platform-tabs:has(> .platform-tabs-marker[data-marker-at]) .platform-rail-row:has(> .platform-rail-community[data-rail-open][aria-current="page"]):not(:has(+ .platform-rail-nest:not([data-nest="closing"]) :is(.dev-ws-place, .platform-rail-sub)[aria-current="page"])) > .platform-rail-pin {
    color: var(--wip-nav-on-ink);
    --lit-ink: var(--wip-nav-on-ink);
    --lit-tint: var(--wip-nav-on-pin-hover);
    --accent: var(--wip-nav-on-ink);
  }
}

/* THE SIDEBAR'S HEADINGS (Recents, Pinned) ARE THE SECTION LABEL (design review, 25 Nov 2026): 12px bold capitals,
   tracked 0.06em, in the panel's muted white, starting where the rows' glyphs do, as every label over a group is
   (AGENTS.md, "Type and colour"). They had been set in sentence case at 12.5/600. A community's own sub-headers
   (Channels, Topics) stay in sentence case: they are a level down. */
@media (min-width: 768px) {
  html:root #platform-tabs :is(.platform-rail-head, .platform-rail-head-label) { text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.06em; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; }
  html:root #platform-tabs .platform-rail-head { padding-inline: var(--wip-nav-row-pad) 8px; }
}

/* THE TOP BAR, ONE STYLE ON EVERY PAGE (design review, 25 Nov 2026). On a phone its title was 16/600 on Communities,
   Homeroom bot, You, Settings, Challenges and a project's page and 17/650 on Messages, a conversation and a request
   (the drawer's titles, ../nav-drawer/header-drawer.tsx): now every page's is 17/600 in the bar's white, and the line
   under it (a conversation's "Direct message", a project's place) 12/500 at 82%. Homeroom's logotype on Home is drawn
   at the mock's 24px. The back disc on the blue bar is a plain white disc with the ink chevron: 36px, no edge, no
   translucent fill. (Android keeps its bare arrow, overnight audit G01.) The bell and the Homeroom menu stay on every
   page; nothing here hides them. From 768px the bar stands on the page, so its title is the page's ink at the same
   17/600, the place under a project's name 12/500 in the quiet ink, and the back is the flat disc (white, one
   hairline). */
@media (max-width: 767.98px) {
  html:root #platform-header :is(#header-title-name, .nav-drawer-title-name) { font-size: 17px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
  html:root #platform-header :is(#header-subtitle, .nav-drawer-title-page) { font-size: 12px; font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: 0; color: color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 82%, transparent); }
  html:root #platform-header #header-title-name > svg { width: 93px; height: 24px; }
  html:root:not(.un-android) #platform-header #back-btn,
  html:root #platform-header .nav-drawer-back {
    width: 36px;
    height: 36px;
    border: 0;
    background: var(--one-back-bg);
    box-shadow: none;
    color: var(--one-back-ink);
  }
  html:root:not(.un-android) #platform-header #back-btn > svg,
  html:root #platform-header .nav-drawer-back > svg { width: 20px; height: 20px; stroke-width: 2.2; }
  html:root:not(.un-android) #platform-header #back-btn:active,
  html:root #platform-header .nav-drawer-back:active { filter: var(--one-flat-dim); }
  /* Beside the disc the bar steps in as the mock draws it: the disc 8px from the screen's edge (the bar's own 16px
     less 8) and the title 6px after it (the bar's 16px gap less 10). The drawer measures its titles' slot from the
     laid-out group, so its names follow. */
  html:root:not(.un-android) #platform-header .platform-header-left:has(> #back-btn:not(.hidden)),
  html:root #platform-header .platform-header-left:has(> .nav-drawer-back) { margin-inline: -8px -10px; }
  /* 48px under the status bar, the controls in its middle (design review, 25 Nov 2026): 10 over the 28px row and
     10 under it, where the flat blue bar (Mobile 01) had 12 and 12 (52px). Both bars move together, so the
     header-height invariant (#909, "Header height invariant" above) still holds, and --platform-header-h says the
     new height. The doubled id and the body:has() outrank Mobile 01's per-screen rules and the tinted bar's
     (#4237), which are (2,2,2) and (2,3,2). */
  html:root { --platform-header-h: 3rem; }
  html:root body:has(:is(#platform-header, #landing-header)) :is(#platform-header#platform-header, #landing-header#landing-header) { padding-bottom: 10px; }
  html:root #platform-header { padding-inline-end: 10px; }
  /* The bell is the mock's: 21px at a 1.8 stroke, centred on the same 28px box. The Homeroom mark is 28px, 14px
     after the bell, its chevron 12px from the screen's edge. */
  html:root #platform-header #notifications-btn > svg { width: 21px; height: 21px; }
  html:root #platform-header > .ms-auto { gap: 14px; }
  html:root #platform-header #platform-mark-btn .platform-mark-tile { width: 28px; height: 28px; border-radius: 8px; }
}
@media (max-width: 767.98px) {
  @supports (padding: env(safe-area-inset-top)) {
    html:root body:has(:is(#platform-header, #landing-header)) :is(#platform-header#platform-header, #landing-header#landing-header).un-safe-top-extend {
      padding-top: calc(10px + var(--un-safe-inset-top, env(safe-area-inset-top, 0px))) !important;
    }
    html.web-browser-chrome:root body:has(:is(#platform-header, #landing-header)) :is(#platform-header#platform-header, #landing-header#landing-header).un-safe-top-extend { padding-top: 10px !important; }
  }
}
/* Every bar's bell, phone and desktop, at the mock's 1.8 stroke (it was 2). */
html:root #platform-header #notifications-btn > svg { stroke-width: 1.8; }
@media (min-width: 768px) {
  html:root #platform-header #header-title-name,
  html:root #platform-header #header-title > span > span:has(> .header-place-name) > #header-title-name { color: var(--one-ink); font-size: 17px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
  html:root #platform-header :is(#header-subtitle, .header-place-name) { color: var(--one-ink-2); font-size: 12px; font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: 0; opacity: 1; }
  /* Homeroom's own place alone, beside the open sidebar, is the bar's title (20/700 before): the same 17/600. */
  html:root body:has(> #platform-tabs:not(.hidden):not(.platform-tabs-route-hidden):not(.platform-tabs-folded)) #platform-header #header-title > span:has(> span > #header-title-name > svg) .header-place-name { color: var(--one-ink); font-size: 17px; font-weight: 600; line-height: 1.4; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
  /* A project's Suggest is a secondary action on the bar: flat, the sky tint with the sky's words. */
  html:root #platform-header #header-in-app-suggest { border-color: transparent; background: var(--one-sky-tint); color: var(--one-sky-ink); }
  html:root #platform-header #header-in-app-suggest:active { transform: var(--one-flat-press); filter: var(--one-flat-dim); }
  html:root #platform-header #back-btn {
    width: 34px;
    height: 34px;
    border: 0;
    background: var(--one-surface);
    box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--one-field-line);
    color: var(--one-ink);
  }  html:root #platform-header .platform-header-left:has(> #back-btn:not(.hidden)) { margin-inline-end: -4px; }
}
/* A SECTION'S OWN ACTION (design review, 25 Nov 2026). The words after a section's label (Edit and Done, See all,
   Show all, All in Workshop, View all activity) are the label row's own ink at 14/600, with no underline and no
   chevron: the label beside them already says what they act on, so they need no more than their weight. An action
   inside a card's words (Translate, Read the request, Change, Cancel) keeps the blue underline (the BUTTONS block's
   level 4). */
html:root :is(.home-edit-start, #communities-edit, .wip-fold-pill, #profile-recent-activity .profile-recent-heading > a):is(button, a, span) {
  color: var(--one-ink);
  font-size: 14px;
  font-weight: 600;
  text-decoration: none;
}
html:root .wip-fold-pill > .wip-head-chevron-glyph { display: none; }
/* ── END ONE LOOK · SHARED PARTS ── */

/* ── ONE LOOK · HOMEROOM BOT AND NEW CHAT ── */
/* The Homeroom bot tab (features/ai/lists.tsx and index.tsx) and New chat
   (features/messages/new-thread.tsx), drawn with the shared parts above:
   the head card kept (the mark, the counts with Needs you as a text action,
   the sun + as the fab, the search field and the All projects menu chip),
   today's tinted Needs you band at the top of its card, rows on the ramp
   with their project tiles and a tag at their end, and on a phone the list
   running on under the Ask box to the tab bar. New chat: the five starts as
   flat white chips, About and With as menu chips, the message box with the
   sun send; a title card and then one card at every width, and Live preview
   in the title card once About is a project (26 Nov 2026, below). */

/* ── The cards: white, 20px, one hairline; 10px between them. ── */
html:root #ai-screen .ai-lists { gap: 10px; }
html:root #ai-screen .ai-lists > [data-ai-sheet],
html:root #ai-screen .ai-lists > :is([data-ai-search-empty], [data-ai-search-failed]) {
  background: var(--one-surface);
  border-radius: 20px;
  box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--one-hair);
}

/* ── The head card: the mark, the counts and the +; then search and the menu chip. ── */
/* The card is one column that can be narrower than its contents' min-content
   (request #7231): an implicit auto track is as wide as the search field's
   own width, which put the + and All projects past the card at the 280px
   list floor. minmax(0, 1fr) lets the track be the card, and the two lines'
   own min-width: 0 lets them wrap instead of overflowing. */
html:root #ai-screen [data-ai-sheet="head"] { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 10px; padding: 12px; }
html:root #ai-screen [data-ai-sheet="head"] > :is([data-ai-hero], [data-ai-tools]) { padding: 0; min-width: 0; }
html:root #ai-screen [data-ai-hero] { gap: 10px; }
html:root #ai-screen [data-ai-hero] > img { width: 40px; height: 40px; border-radius: 10px; }
/* The mark keeps its place down to a 250px line (the 320px card beside a thread), as the design review drew it. */
@container (max-width: 299.98px) {
  html:root #ai-screen [data-ai-hero] > img { display: block; }
}
@container (max-width: 249.98px) {
  html:root #ai-screen [data-ai-hero] > img { display: none; }
}
html:root #ai-screen [data-ai-hero-sub] { font-size: 14px; line-height: 20px; color: var(--one-ink-2); }
/* "Needs you: 25": what asks for you, in the ink, as a text action (underlined in the blue). */
html:root #ai-screen [data-ai-hero-sub] > :is(button, strong) {
  font-size: 16px; font-weight: 650; color: var(--one-ink);
}
html:root #ai-screen [data-ai-hero-sub] > button {
  text-decoration: underline; text-decoration-color: #3090e1; text-decoration-thickness: 1.5px; text-underline-offset: 4px;
}
html:root #ai-screen [data-ai-hero-sub] > button:hover { color: var(--one-ink); text-decoration-thickness: 2px; }
/* The + is the page's main action: the shared fab, at its size whatever the button's own variant says. */
html:root #ai-screen [data-ai-hero] [data-ai-new-chat].one-fab { min-width: 40px; color: #121a0e; }
html:root #ai-screen [data-ai-hero] [data-ai-new-chat].one-fab:hover { background: var(--one-sun); filter: brightness(.97); }
html:root #ai-screen [data-ai-hero] [data-ai-new-chat].one-fab > svg { width: 21px; height: 21px; stroke-width: 2.1; }
html:root #ai-screen [data-ai-hero] [data-ai-new-chat].one-fab:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--accent); outline-offset: 2px; }
html:root #ai-screen [data-ai-tools] { gap: 10px; }
/* The search field: a white pill with the field's hairline. */
html:root #ai-screen [data-ai-search-box] {
  flex: 1 1 8rem; min-width: 7rem; height: 40px; gap: 8px; padding-inline: 12px 14px;
  border-radius: 9999px; background: var(--one-surface); color: var(--one-ink-3);
  box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--one-field-line);
}
html:root #ai-screen [data-ai-search-box]:focus-within { box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 2px var(--accent); }
html:root #ai-screen [data-ai-search-box] > svg:first-child { width: 19px; height: 19px; }
/* The field's own width (about 20 characters) is no floor: it grows only by
   flex-1, so the search can be as narrow as the label's 7rem. */
html:root #ai-screen [data-ai-search-box] > input { width: 0; font-size: 16px; color: var(--one-ink); }
html:root #ai-screen [data-ai-search-box] > input::placeholder { color: var(--one-ink-3); }
/* All projects: the shared menu chip. It says what it shows, so no filter glyph before it; a picked project keeps its tile. */
html:root #ai-screen [data-ai-project-more].one-chip { flex: 0 1 auto; min-width: 0; max-width: 100%; }
html:root #ai-screen [data-ai-project-more].one-chip:hover:not(:disabled) { background: var(--one-surface); }
html:root #ai-screen [data-ai-project-more].one-chip:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--accent); outline-offset: 2px; }
html:root #ai-screen [data-ai-project-more].one-chip:disabled { color: var(--one-ink-3); }
html:root #ai-screen [data-ai-project-more] > .ai-filter-glyph { display: none; }
html:root #ai-screen [data-ai-project-more] > svg:last-child { width: 15px; height: 15px; stroke-width: 2; color: var(--one-ink); }

/* ── A band's strip, as today: Needs you tinted in the sky, the others quiet. ── */
html:root #ai-screen [data-ai-band] { min-height: 42px; gap: 8px; padding: 0 12px; border-radius: 14px; background: var(--one-quiet); color: var(--one-ink); }
html:root #ai-screen :is([data-ai-list="work"], [data-ai-list="waiting"]) > [data-ai-band] { background: var(--one-sky-tint); color: var(--one-sky-ink); }
html:root #ai-screen [data-ai-band] > h3 { gap: 8px; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 650; line-height: 20px; }
html:root #ai-screen [data-ai-band] > h3 > span:first-child > svg { width: 19px; height: 19px; }
html:root #ai-screen [data-ai-band-count] {
  height: auto; min-width: 0; padding: 4px 8px; border-radius: 9999px;
  background: var(--one-surface); font-size: 13px; font-weight: 700; line-height: 1; color: var(--one-ink-2);
}
html:root #ai-screen :is([data-ai-list="work"], [data-ai-list="waiting"]) [data-ai-band-count] { color: var(--one-sky-ink); }
html:root #ai-screen [data-ai-band] [data-ai-band-aside] { color: inherit; opacity: .8; }

/* ── The rows: the project's tile, the title over its second line (16/14, 15/13 from 768px), a tag at the end, one line between. ── */
html:root #ai-screen .ai-lists [data-ai-row] { position: relative; }
html:root #ai-screen .ai-lists [data-ai-row] + [data-ai-row]::before,
html:root #ai-screen .ai-lists [data-ai-row] + [data-ai-group-rest] > div > [data-ai-row]:first-child::before,
html:root #ai-screen .ai-lists :is([data-ai-row], [data-ai-group-rest]) + :is([data-ai-group-more], [data-ai-history-more])::before {
  content: ""; position: absolute; top: 0; inset-inline-start: 52px; inset-inline-end: -6px; height: 1px;
  background: var(--one-line); pointer-events: none;
}
html:root #ai-screen .ai-lists [data-ai-row] > div > [data-ai-line] { min-height: 44px; gap: 12px; padding: 10px 8px; }
html:root #ai-screen .ai-lists [data-ai-line] > [data-ai-dot] { inset-inline-start: -2px; }
html:root #ai-screen .ai-lists [data-ai-line] > :is(.app-icon-tile, .ai-row-tile) { width: 32px; height: 32px; border-radius: 9px; }
html:root #ai-screen .ai-lists [data-ai-line] > .ai-row-tile { background: var(--one-quiet); color: var(--one-ink-2); }
html:root #ai-screen .ai-lists [data-ai-line] > .ai-row-tile > svg { width: 16px; height: 16px; }
html:root #ai-screen .ai-lists [data-ai-line] > .app-icon-tile[data-icon="emoji"] { background-color: var(--one-surface); border-color: var(--one-line); }
html:root #ai-screen .ai-lists [data-ai-line] > .app-icon-tile[data-icon="emoji"] > span { font-size: 18px; }
html:root #ai-screen .ai-lists [data-ai-line] > .app-icon-tile[data-icon="letter"] { font-size: 14px; }
html:root #ai-screen .ai-lists [data-ai-line-title] { font-size: 16px; line-height: 21px; }
html:root #ai-screen .ai-lists [data-ai-line]:not([data-ai-fresh]) [data-ai-line-title] { font-weight: 600; }
html:root #ai-screen .ai-lists :is([data-ai-line-why], [data-ai-line-where]) { margin-top: 2px; font-size: 14px; line-height: 19px; color: var(--one-ink-2); }
html:root #ai-screen .ai-lists [data-ai-line]:not([data-ai-lit]) [data-ai-line-title] { color: var(--one-ink); }
/* Dismiss keeps its own 44px target beside Reply; it is drawn as a quiet tag. */
html:root #ai-screen .ai-lists [data-ai-dismiss] {
  position: relative; isolation: isolate; margin-inline-start: 2px; padding-inline: 9px;
  background: transparent; color: var(--one-ink-2); font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600;
}
html:root #ai-screen .ai-lists [data-ai-dismiss]::before {
  content: ""; position: absolute; z-index: -1; inset-inline: 0; top: 50%; height: 24px; margin-top: -12px;
  border-radius: 9999px; background: var(--one-quiet);
}
html:root #ai-screen .ai-lists [data-ai-dismiss]:hover { background: transparent; color: var(--one-ink); }
html:root #ai-screen .ai-lists [data-ai-dismiss]:last-of-type { margin-inline-end: 8px; }
/* Show N more: a text action, the ink underlined in the blue. */
html:root #ai-screen .ai-lists :is([data-ai-group-more], [data-ai-history-more]) {
  position: relative; font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--one-ink);
}
html:root #ai-screen .ai-lists :is([data-ai-group-more], [data-ai-history-more]) {
  text-decoration: underline; text-decoration-color: #3090e1; text-decoration-thickness: 1.5px; text-underline-offset: 4px;
}
html:root #ai-screen .ai-lists :is([data-ai-group-more], [data-ai-history-more]):hover { background: transparent; color: var(--one-ink); text-decoration-thickness: 2px; }
html:root #ai-screen .ai-lists :is([data-ai-group-more], [data-ai-history-more]) > svg { color: var(--one-ink-2); }
@media (min-width: 768px) {
  html:root #ai-screen [data-ai-sheet="head"] { padding: 12px 14px; }
  html:root #ai-screen [data-ai-hero-sub] { font-size: 13px; }
  html:root #ai-screen [data-ai-hero-sub] > :is(button, strong) { font-size: 15px; }
  html:root #ai-screen [data-ai-hero] [data-ai-new-chat].one-fab { width: 36px; height: 36px; min-width: 36px; }
  html:root #ai-screen [data-ai-search-box] { height: 36px; }
  html:root #ai-screen [data-ai-search-box] > input { font-size: 15px; }
  html:root #ai-screen [data-ai-search-box] > svg:first-child { width: 17px; height: 17px; }
  html:root #ai-screen [data-ai-project-more].one-chip { height: 30px; font-size: 13px; padding-inline: 12px 9px; }
  html:root #ai-screen .ai-lists [data-ai-row] > div > [data-ai-line] { min-height: 40px; padding-block: 8px; }
  html:root #ai-screen .ai-lists [data-ai-line-title] { font-size: 15px; line-height: 20px; }
  html:root #ai-screen .ai-lists :is([data-ai-line-why], [data-ai-line-where]) { margin-top: 0; font-size: 13px; line-height: 18px; }
  html:root #ai-screen .ai-lists :is([data-ai-group-more], [data-ai-history-more]) { font-size: 14px; }
}
/* With the room for its words (the list dragged past 520px) the + is a sun pill with them, as New chat was. */
@container ai-list (min-width: 520px) {
  html:root #ai-screen [data-ai-hero] [data-ai-new-chat].one-fab { display: inline-flex; gap: 6px; width: auto; padding-inline: 14px 16px; }
}
/* The wide row's project column (the list dragged past 520px) on the same ramp. */
@container ai-list (min-width: 520px) {
  html:root #ai-screen .ai-lists [data-ai-row-project] > :first-child { font-size: 14px; line-height: 19px; color: var(--one-ink); }
  html:root #ai-screen .ai-lists [data-ai-row-project] > [data-ai-line-number] { font-size: 13px; line-height: 18px; color: var(--one-ink-2); }
}

/* ── The Ask box on a phone: the message box it opens (+, words, mic, the quiet send), floating over the list. ── */
html:root #ai-screen .ai-askbar { padding: 8px 12px; }
html:root #ai-screen .ai-askbar-card {
  min-height: 48px; gap: 4px; padding: 0 6px; border-radius: 9999px; background: var(--one-surface);
  box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--one-field-line), 0 6px 18px -10px rgb(18 26 14 / 0.35);
}
html:root #ai-screen .ai-askbar-card:focus-visible { outline: none; box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 2px var(--accent), 0 6px 18px -10px rgb(18 26 14 / 0.35); }
html:root #ai-screen .ai-askbar-text { padding: 0 4px; font-size: 16px; line-height: 20px; color: var(--one-ink-3); }
html:root #ai-screen .ai-askbar-card > .messages-composer-action { width: 36px; height: 36px; color: var(--one-ink-2); }
html:root #ai-screen .ai-askbar-send {
  display: inline-grid; place-items: center; flex: none; width: 36px; height: 36px; border-radius: 9999px;
  background: var(--one-quiet); color: var(--one-ink-3);
}
html:root #ai-screen .ai-askbar-send > svg { width: 19px; height: 19px; stroke-width: 2.2; }
/* THE LIST RUNS ON UNDER THE BOX TO THE TAB BAR. On the phone's drawer the
   box is sticky at the list's foot (the earlier rule, ON THE TAB BAR, NOT
   UNDER IT); here it lays its height and the tab bar's over the list's end
   rather than after it, and the last card reaches to the screen's foot with
   room inside it for its last row to scroll clear of the box. A short list's
   last card runs on to the foot as well. */
html:root #ai-screen .ai-drawer-list { --one-ask-h: 64px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; }
html:root #ai-screen .ai-drawer-list > .ai-screen-body { display: flex; flex-direction: column; flex: 1 0 auto; width: 100%; padding-bottom: 0; }
html:root #ai-screen .ai-drawer-list .ai-lists { flex: 1 0 auto; padding-top: 20px; }
html:root #ai-screen .ai-drawer-list .ai-lists > :last-child {
  flex-grow: 1;
  padding-bottom: calc(var(--one-ask-h) + var(--platform-tabs-h, 0px) + 12px);
}
html:root #ai-screen .ai-drawer-list .ai-askbar {
  flex: none;
  margin-top: calc(-1 * (var(--one-ask-h) + var(--platform-tabs-h, 0px)));
}

/* ── New chat: the bot's mark and question, the five starts as flat chips, About and With, the message box. ── */
html:root [data-bot-new-thread-pane] .messages-starts { gap: 10px; }
html:root [data-bot-new-thread-pane] .messages-starts-hello { gap: 8px; margin-bottom: 18px; }
html:root [data-bot-new-thread-pane] .messages-starts-hello > img { width: 46px; height: 46px; margin-bottom: 0; border-radius: 12px; }
html:root [data-bot-new-thread-pane] .messages-starts-title { font-size: 22px; line-height: 1.2; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.015em; color: var(--one-ink); }
html:root [data-bot-new-thread-pane] .messages-starts-sub { font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.35; color: var(--one-ink-2); }
/* Each start its own width, the stack centred. */
html:root [data-bot-new-thread-pane] .messages-starts-list { display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; gap: 10px; }
html:root [data-bot-new-thread-pane] .messages-start {
  min-height: 44px; gap: 10px; padding-block: 0; padding-inline: 14px 18px;
  background: var(--one-surface); color: var(--one-ink);
  box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--one-field-line);
  font-size: 16px; line-height: 20px; font-weight: 400;
}
html:root [data-bot-new-thread-pane] .messages-start > svg { width: 19px; height: 19px; color: var(--one-ink); }
html:root [data-bot-new-thread-pane] .messages-start:hover { background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--one-ink) 4%, var(--one-surface)); }
html:root [data-bot-new-thread-pane] .messages-start[aria-pressed="true"] { box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--one-field-line), 0 0 0 2px var(--accent); }
html:root [data-bot-new-thread-pane] .messages-start-more { color: var(--one-ink-3); }
/* About and With: the shared menu chips, over the box. */
/* Side by side while there is room; in a narrow column With goes under About rather than out of the card. */
html:root [data-bot-new-thread-pane] .messages-project-row { flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; padding-bottom: 6px; }
html:root [data-bot-new-thread-pane] .messages-project-chip.one-chip { min-width: 0; max-width: 100%; transition: none; }
html:root [data-bot-new-thread-pane] .messages-project-chip.one-chip:has(> .messages-project-chip-tile) { padding-inline-start: 6px; }
html:root [data-bot-new-thread-pane] .messages-project-chip.one-chip:hover { background: var(--one-surface); }
html:root [data-bot-new-thread-pane] .messages-project-chip.one-chip:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--accent); outline-offset: 2px; }
html:root [data-bot-new-thread-pane] .messages-project-chip.one-chip .one-chip-lead { font-weight: 400; color: var(--one-ink-2); }
html:root [data-bot-new-thread-pane] .messages-project-chip.one-chip .messages-project-chip-chev { width: 15px; height: 15px; stroke-width: 2; color: var(--one-ink); }
/* The message box: a white pill with the field's hairline, lifted a little. */
html:root [data-bot-new-thread-pane] .messages-composer-card {
  min-height: 48px; padding-block: 6px; padding-inline: 6px 6px; border-radius: 24px; background: var(--one-surface);
  box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--one-field-line), 0 6px 18px -10px rgb(18 26 14 / 0.35);
}
html:root [data-bot-new-thread-pane] .messages-composer-card:focus-within {
  box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 2px var(--accent), 0 6px 18px -10px rgb(18 26 14 / 0.35);
}
html:root [data-bot-new-thread-pane] .messages-composer-row { align-items: center; }
html:root [data-bot-new-thread-pane] .messages-composer-input { font-size: 16px; }
/* The box's question stays on its one line, cut at the box's edge (with an ellipsis where the browser draws one in a
   textarea): in a 320px column it wrapped onto a second line under the box's foot. */
html:root [data-bot-new-thread-pane] .messages-composer-input::placeholder { color: var(--one-ink-3); white-space: nowrap; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; }
html:root [data-bot-new-thread-pane] .messages-composer-action { color: var(--one-ink-2); }
/* Send: the sun disc once there is something to send (flat, no edge), a quiet grey disc until then. */
html:root [data-bot-new-thread-pane] .messages-send {
  width: 36px; height: 36px; background: var(--one-sun); color: #121a0e; box-shadow: none; opacity: 1;
}
html:root [data-bot-new-thread-pane] .messages-send:hover:not(:disabled) { background: var(--one-sun); filter: brightness(.96); }
html:root [data-bot-new-thread-pane] .messages-send svg { width: 19px; height: 19px; stroke-width: 2.2; }
html:root [data-bot-new-thread-pane] .messages-composer-card .messages-send:disabled,
html:root [data-bot-new-thread-pane] .messages-composer-card:not([data-gc-files]):has(textarea:placeholder-shown) .messages-send:not(.messages-send-open) {
  background: var(--one-quiet); color: var(--one-ink-3); opacity: 1;
}
html:root [data-bot-new-thread-pane] .messages-send.messages-send-open { width: auto; }
@media (min-width: 768px) {
  html:root [data-bot-new-thread-pane] .messages-start { font-size: 16px; }
  html:root [data-bot-new-thread-pane] .messages-project-chip.one-chip { height: 30px; font-size: 13px; }
  html:root [data-bot-new-thread-pane] .messages-composer-card { min-height: 44px; padding-block: 4px; }
  html:root [data-bot-new-thread-pane] .messages-composer-input { font-size: 15px; }
}

/* A TITLE CARD, THEN ONE CARD, AT EVERY WIDTH (26 Nov 2026). New chat is
   drawn as a thread is, and as a Messages conversation is: a title card that
   names it ("New chat" over who it is with), then one card holding the
   starts, About and With and the message box, 10px under it, on the wash.
   It was one card with its head inside from 768px, and on a phone no card
   at all under a bar that named it. */
/* On a phone, in the bot tab's drawer: the same two cards. The bar says the
   tab's name beside its back disc (features/ai/new-chat-bar.ts), and the
   title card names the chat. The card is the pane's own `::before`, laid over
   the rows under the head, as the docked column's is (NEW CHAT IS DRAWN AS
   CARDS). */
html:root #ai-screen .ai-drawer-thread:has(> .ai-drawer-pane [data-bot-new-thread-pane]) { background: var(--home-washes, var(--home-ground)); }
html:root #ai-screen .ai-drawer [data-bot-new-thread-pane] {
  --thread-gutter: 12px;
  --thread-card-r: 20px;
  display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); grid-template-rows: auto minmax(0, 1fr) auto; isolation: isolate;
  /* The card ends over the tab bar and the home indicator, as a Messages conversation's does: the pane clears
     them, not the message bar inside the card (below). */
  padding: 12px 0 calc(max(var(--platform-tabs-h, 0px), var(--platform-safe-bottom, 0px)) + 12px);
  background: transparent; box-shadow: none; backdrop-filter: none; -webkit-backdrop-filter: none;
}
html.un-kb:root #ai-screen .ai-drawer [data-bot-new-thread-pane],
html.platform-kb-open:root #ai-screen .ai-drawer [data-bot-new-thread-pane] {
  padding-bottom: calc(var(--un-kb-inset, 0px) + 8px);
}
html:root #ai-screen .ai-drawer [data-bot-new-thread-pane]::before {
  content: ""; grid-row: 2 / -1; grid-column: 1; z-index: -1;
  margin: 10px var(--thread-gutter) 0; border-radius: var(--thread-card-r);
  background: var(--one-surface); box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--one-hair);
}
html:root #ai-screen .ai-drawer [data-bot-new-thread-pane] > * { grid-column: 1; }
html:root #ai-screen .ai-drawer [data-bot-new-thread-pane] > .messages-thread-header {
  position: relative; inset: auto; grid-row: 1; gap: 12px; min-height: 68px; margin-inline: var(--thread-gutter); padding: 12px 14px;
  border-radius: var(--thread-card-r); background: var(--one-surface); box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--one-hair);
}
html:root #ai-screen .ai-drawer [data-bot-new-thread-pane] > .messages-thread-header .messages-thread-name { font-size: 19px; font-weight: 700; line-height: 24px; letter-spacing: -0.012em; color: var(--one-ink); }
html:root #ai-screen .ai-drawer [data-bot-new-thread-pane] > .messages-thread-header .messages-thread-sub { overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; white-space: nowrap; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 400; line-height: 18px; color: var(--one-ink-2); }
html:root #ai-screen .ai-drawer [data-bot-new-thread-pane] > :is(.messages-thread-scroll, .messages-builder-setup) { grid-row: 2; margin: 10px var(--thread-gutter) 0; }
html:root #ai-screen .ai-drawer [data-bot-new-thread-pane] > .messages-composer { grid-row: 3; margin: 0 var(--thread-gutter); padding: 0 6px 8px !important; }
/* About and With share the card's line, a little closer set than from 768px so both fit a 390px phone; a longer
   project's name gives way with an ellipsis before the row runs out of the card. */
html:root #ai-screen .ai-drawer [data-bot-new-thread-pane] .messages-project-row { min-width: 0; gap: 6px; }
html:root #ai-screen .ai-drawer [data-bot-new-thread-pane] .messages-project-chip.one-chip { padding-inline: 10px 8px; font-size: 13px; }
html:root #ai-screen .ai-drawer [data-bot-new-thread-pane] .messages-project-chip.one-chip:has(> .messages-project-chip-tile) { padding-inline-start: 5px; }
html:root #ai-screen .ai-drawer [data-bot-new-thread-pane] .messages-project-chip.one-chip[data-bot-new-thread-project] { flex: 0 1 auto; }
html:root #ai-screen .ai-drawer [data-bot-new-thread-pane] .messages-project-chip-name { min-width: 0; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; white-space: nowrap; }
html:root #ai-screen .ai-drawer [data-bot-new-thread-pane] .messages-starts { gap: 14px; padding: 16px 4px 12px; }
html:root #ai-screen .ai-drawer [data-bot-new-thread-pane] .messages-starts-hello { margin-bottom: 0; }
/* The bar's back disc while New chat is up is the shared one (SHARED PARTS, THE TOP BAR), and the tab's name is alone
   on its line beside it, as "Messages" is over a conversation. */
html:root body:has(#ai-screen:not(.hidden)) #platform-header .nav-drawer-title:has(> .nav-drawer-title-page:empty) { margin-top: -10px; }

/* From 768px, docked beside the list: the title card and the card under it are white with the one hairline. */
html:root #ai-screen .ai-main-pane .messages-layout > [data-bot-new-thread-docked] {
  --thread-card: var(--one-surface);
  --thread-card-solid: var(--one-surface);
  --thread-card-edge: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--one-hair);
}
html:root #ai-screen .ai-main-pane .messages-layout > [data-bot-new-thread-docked]::before { margin-top: 10px; }
html:root #ai-screen .ai-main-pane .messages-layout > [data-bot-new-thread-docked] > .messages-thread-header {
  gap: 12px; margin-inline: var(--thread-gutter); padding-block: 12px; padding-inline: 14px calc(14px + var(--ai-edge, 0px));
}
html:root #ai-screen .ai-main-pane .messages-layout > [data-bot-new-thread-docked] > .messages-thread-header .messages-thread-name { font-size: 17px; font-weight: 600; line-height: 1.2; color: var(--one-ink); }
html:root #ai-screen .ai-main-pane .messages-layout > [data-bot-new-thread-docked] > .messages-thread-header .messages-thread-sub { font-size: 12px; font-weight: 500; line-height: 1.3; color: var(--one-ink-2); }
html:root #ai-screen .ai-main-pane .messages-layout > [data-bot-new-thread-docked] > :is(.messages-thread-scroll, .messages-builder-setup) { margin-top: 10px; }
html:root #ai-screen .ai-main-pane .messages-layout > [data-bot-new-thread-docked] .messages-starts { gap: 14px; }
html:root #ai-screen .ai-main-pane .messages-layout > [data-bot-new-thread-docked] .messages-starts-hello { margin-bottom: 0; }
html:root #ai-screen .ai-main-pane .messages-layout > [data-bot-new-thread-docked] > .messages-composer { margin-bottom: 8px; padding-inline: max(14px, calc((100% - 720px) / 2 - var(--thread-gutter))); }
html:root #ai-screen .ai-main-pane .messages-layout > [data-bot-new-thread-docked] .messages-composer-card { margin-bottom: 14px; }

/* ── Start live preview (26 Nov 2026; features/messages/new-thread.tsx START LIVE PREVIEW). ── */
/* In New chat's title card, once About is a project whose app can be changed live: a secondary action, flat in the
   sky tint, so Send stays the one sun. */
html:root [data-bot-new-thread-pane] .messages-live-start {
  display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px; flex: none; height: 36px; padding: 0 14px 0 11px; border: 0; border-radius: 9999px;
  background: var(--one-sky-tint); color: var(--one-sky-ink); box-shadow: none;
  font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; line-height: 1; white-space: nowrap;
}
html:root [data-bot-new-thread-pane] .messages-live-start > svg { width: 17px; height: 17px; flex: none; }
html:root [data-bot-new-thread-pane] .messages-live-start:active:not(:disabled) { transform: var(--one-flat-press); filter: var(--one-flat-dim); }
html:root [data-bot-new-thread-pane] .messages-live-start:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--one-link-line); outline-offset: 2px; }
html:root [data-bot-new-thread-pane] .messages-live-start:disabled { opacity: .45; cursor: not-allowed; }
@media (hover: hover) {
  html:root [data-bot-new-thread-pane] .messages-live-start:hover:not(:disabled) { background: var(--one-sky-tint-hover); }
}
/* WAITING, THE COLUMN HAS WIDTHS OF ITS OWN (27 Nov 2026). A real preview keeps the widths its edges were dragged
   to, and people drag it wide: the app is what they look at, and the thread beside it is left at its 320px floor.
   Those same widths under a column that is only waiting gave New chat 320px beside 860px of empty outline. The first
   fix clamped the waiting column to the chat's width, which tied the two edges together: dragging one moved the
   other, and neither followed the pointer past its clamp. So while it waits (`data-ai-live-wait`, features/ai/
   index.tsx) the two edges remember widths of their own (`--ai-live-col-chosen-w`, `--ai-live-preview-chosen-w`,
   features/side-panel/resize.ts), in the rules a real preview's follow, floors and all, so each drags as a
   preview's does.
   NEVER DRAGGED, THEY USE ALL OF THE ROOM (27 Nov 2026). They started at 440px each with the list taking the rest,
   but the list is held to 42rem (`--ai-list-max`, THE THREAD TAKES THE SPARE ROOM), so on a wide window the rest
   was an empty band between the list and New chat (about 90px at 1900px). The starting widths give that room away:
   the column 440px, New chat whatever the list's 42rem and the column do not need, never under 440px. Past New
   chat's 720px reading measure ("A WIDER COLUMN KEEPS A READABLE LINE") the column takes the rest instead. These
   are only the widths nothing was chosen for: a dragged width is kept as dragged, and New chat's start follows the
   column's width, so dragging the column's edge alone shares the room between the two and leaves the list be. */
body:has(#ai-screen[data-ai-preview="three"][data-ai-live-wait]:not(.hidden)) {
  --ai-preview-w: max(360px, min(var(--ai-live-preview-chosen-w, max(min(440px, calc(var(--ai-room) - 920px)), calc(var(--ai-room) - var(--ai-list-max, 42rem) - 720px))), calc(var(--ai-room) - 800px)));
  --ai-col-w: max(320px, min(var(--ai-live-col-chosen-w, max(min(var(--ai-main-w), 440px), calc(var(--ai-room) - var(--ai-list-max, 42rem) - var(--ai-preview-w)))), calc(var(--ai-room) - 480px - var(--ai-preview-w))));
}
body:has(#ai-screen[data-ai-preview="halves"][data-ai-live-wait]:not(.hidden)) {
  --ai-preview-w: max(320px, min(var(--ai-live-preview-chosen-w, calc(var(--ai-room) / 2)), calc(var(--ai-room) - 320px)));
}
body:has(#ai-screen[data-ai-preview="halves"][data-ai-live-wait][data-ai-list-closed]:not(.hidden)) {
  --ai-preview-w: max(320px, min(var(--ai-live-preview-chosen-w, calc(var(--ai-room) / 2)), calc(var(--ai-room) - 16px - 320px)));
}
/* From 1500px the preview's column waits beside New chat instead (features/messages/live-start-pane.tsx), drawn as the
   column's other cards are (.detail-card: a head card, then a card): the project's tile and "Live preview" over where
   it stands, then the words and Start live preview over a faint outline of a screen, or the projects to pick from. */
html:root .live-start-head { flex-wrap: nowrap; gap: 12px; }
html:root .live-start-head-tile { flex: none; width: 36px; height: 36px; border-radius: 11px; }
html:root .live-start-name { margin: 0; font-size: 17px; font-weight: 600; line-height: 1.2; color: var(--one-ink); }
html:root .live-start-sub { margin: 2px 0 0; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; white-space: nowrap; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 500; line-height: 1.3; color: var(--one-ink-2); }
html:root .live-start-body { display: grid; place-items: center; padding: 14px; overflow-y: auto; }
html:root .live-start-ghost {
  position: absolute; inset: 14px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px; padding: 18px; overflow: hidden;
  border: 1px dashed var(--one-field-line); border-radius: 14px; pointer-events: none;
}
html:root .live-start-ghost span { display: block; flex: none; border-radius: 10px; background: var(--one-quiet); opacity: .55; }
html:root .live-start-ghost > div { display: flex; flex: none; gap: 12px; }
html:root .live-start-ghost > div > span { flex: 1 1 0; height: 96px; }
html:root .live-start-cta {
  position: relative; display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; gap: 12px; width: min(360px, 100%); padding: 28px 24px;
  border-radius: 20px; background: var(--one-surface); text-align: center;
}
html:root .live-start-tile { width: 56px; height: 56px; border-radius: 15px; }
html:root .live-start-title { margin: 0; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.25; letter-spacing: -0.012em; color: var(--one-ink); }
html:root .live-start-text { margin: 0; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.4; color: var(--one-ink-2); }
html:root .live-start-note { margin: 0; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.4; color: var(--one-ink-2); }
html:root .live-start-go { margin-top: 6px; }
html:root .live-start-picks { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px; width: min(280px, 100%); margin-top: 6px; }
html:root .live-start-pick {
  display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; width: 100%; min-height: 44px; padding: 0 16px 0 8px; border: 0; border-radius: 9999px;
  background: var(--one-surface); color: var(--one-ink); box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--one-field-line);
  font-size: 16px; line-height: 20px; text-align: start;
}
html:root .live-start-pick:hover { background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--one-ink) 4%, var(--one-surface)); }
html:root .live-start-pick-tile { flex: none; width: 28px; height: 28px; border-radius: 8px; }
html:root .live-start-all {
  display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px; height: 36px; padding: 0 12px 0 14px; border: 0; border-radius: 9999px;
  background: var(--one-sky-tint); color: var(--one-sky-ink); font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; line-height: 1;
}
html:root .live-start-all > svg { width: 15px; height: 15px; }
html:root .live-start-all:hover { background: var(--one-sky-tint-hover); }
html:root :is(.live-start-pick, .live-start-all):focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--one-link-line); outline-offset: 2px; }
/* ── END ONE LOOK · HOMEROOM BOT AND NEW CHAT ── */

/* ── ONE LOOK · MESSAGES AND THREADS ── */
/* Messages and a conversation, and every stream drawn like one (a request's replies, a thread with Homeroom bot):
   features/messages/index.tsx, message-row.tsx, composer.tsx, and features/group-chat/transcript.tsx for a request's
   replies. Shapes are the agreed mockups' (S/mockshots: messages, conversation; request for the replies).
     THE LIST: on the cream wash, never a flush white sheet. The search field and the yellow + (.one-fab) share a row,
       "DMs & groups" heads the rows, and the rows are the shared row in the shared card (ListRow in GroupedList,
       @/components/ui/grouped-list.tsx): nothing of theirs is drawn here.
     A CONVERSATION: a title card (the face, "Direct message" or the group's member line over the name, the discs),
       then ONE white card holding the whole stream with the message bar inside it at its foot. Theirs on the left in
       cream (--one-bubble-in, its first corner square), with the face and the name and the time above; yours on the
       right in sky tint (--one-bubble-out), with only the time. The same on a phone and beside the list on a desktop.
   Everything a conversation does keeps its markup (reactions, threads, files, link cards, the hover bar and the
   long-press sheet, read state, Jump to latest, who is typing, editing): only how it is drawn changes. */

/* ── The list ── */
/* The wash is the page's (the body paints it on every tab root); the drawer's pane no longer covers it in white. */
html:root #messages-screen .messages-layout:not(.messages-layout-embedded),
html:root #messages-screen .messages-layout > .messages-list-pane {
  background: transparent;
  box-shadow: none;
  -webkit-backdrop-filter: none;
  backdrop-filter: none;
}
/* The search row: the field, then the page's main action, the yellow +. */
html:root #messages-screen .messages-list-pane > .messages-toolbar {
  gap: 10px;
  margin: 20px 16px 0;
}
html:root #messages-screen .messages-search-input {
  height: 40px;
  padding-inline: 42px 14px;
  border: 0;
  border-radius: 9999px;
  background: var(--one-surface);
  box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--one-field-line);
  color: var(--one-ink);
  font-size: 16px;
}
html:root #messages-screen .messages-search-input::placeholder { color: var(--one-ink-3); }
html:root #messages-screen .messages-search-input:focus { box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1.5px var(--one-sky); }
html:root #messages-screen .messages-search-glyph { inset-inline-start: 13px; width: 19px; height: 19px; color: var(--one-ink-3); }
/* The + is the shared .one-fab; the old disc's own fill, edge and size give way to it. */
html:root #messages-screen .messages-new-btn.one-fab {
  width: 40px;
  height: 40px;
  border: 0;
  background: var(--one-sun);
  color: #121a0e;
  box-shadow: var(--one-edge);
}
html:root #messages-screen .messages-new-btn.one-fab svg { width: 21px; height: 21px; stroke-width: 2.1; }
html:root #messages-screen .messages-new-btn.one-fab:active:not(:disabled) { box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--one-edge-line); transform: var(--one-press); }
/* "DMs & groups" over the card, and the unread count at its end in the sky ink. */
html:root #messages-screen .messages-list-pane .messages-list-scroll { padding: 0 16px; }
/* WHILE THE LIST IS READ, ITS PLACEHOLDER KEEPS THE HEADING'S PLACE (27 Nov
   2026). The rows that land stand under "DMs & groups", and the placeholder
   rows started where the heading does, so every row dropped by the heading
   (39px on a phone, 40px from 768px) when the list arrived. The placeholder
   now leads with an empty line in the heading's own box: it is named in the
   heading's rules, here and in the 768px one below, so the two cannot drift. */
html:root #messages-screen .messages-list-pane .messages-list-scroll > .animate-pulse::before { content: "\00A0"; display: block; }
html:root #messages-screen .messages-list-pane .messages-section-head,
html:root #messages-screen .messages-list-pane .messages-list-scroll > .animate-pulse::before {
  padding: 15px 6px 8px;
  color: var(--one-ink-2);
  font-size: 12px;
  font-weight: 700;
  letter-spacing: 0.06em;
  line-height: 16px;
}
html:root #messages-screen .messages-list-pane .messages-section-aside {
  color: var(--one-sky-ink);
  font-size: 13px;
  font-weight: 650;
  letter-spacing: 0.04em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
}
/* The list's own states on the wash: an empty inbox is a white card whose Start is the page's main action (the sun
   sticker); a search that found nothing offers its way back as a secondary action, flat in sky tint. */
html:root #messages-screen .messages-list-pane .messages-empty {
  margin: 16px 0 0;
  border-radius: 20px;
  background: var(--one-surface);
  box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--one-hair);
  color: var(--one-ink-2);
}
html:root #messages-screen .messages-list-pane .messages-empty h3 { color: var(--one-ink); }
html:root #messages-screen .messages-list-pane .messages-empty button {
  background: var(--one-sun);
  color: #121a0e;
  box-shadow: var(--one-edge);
}
html:root #messages-screen .messages-list-pane .messages-empty button:active { box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--one-edge-line); transform: var(--one-press); }
html:root #messages-screen .messages-state { color: var(--one-ink-2); }
html:root #messages-screen .messages-state button {
  background: var(--one-sky-tint);
  color: var(--one-sky-ink);
  box-shadow: none;
}
html:root #messages-screen .messages-state button:active { transform: scale(.97); filter: brightness(.95); }

/* ── A conversation: a title card, then the stream's card with the message bar inside it ── */
/* The pane is a column on the wash: no sheet of its own. On a phone it slides in over the list, so it paints the
   wash itself; beside the list it is clear. The stream's card is the pane's ::before, laid over the rows from the
   transcript to the message bar (a grid, so it follows whatever the head and the bar measure, and the scroller's
   own fade under Jump to latest never fades the card). */
html:root #messages-screen .messages-layout:not(.messages-has-reply-thread):not(.messages-has-design) > .messages-thread-pane:not(.messages-no-selection) { display: grid; }
html:root #messages-screen .messages-layout:not(.messages-design-view-preview) > .messages-reply-pane { display: grid; }
@media (min-width: 768px) {
  html:root #messages-screen .messages-layout.messages-has-reply-thread:not(.messages-has-design) > .messages-thread-pane:not(.messages-no-selection) { display: grid; }
  html:root #messages-screen .messages-layout > .messages-reply-pane { display: grid; margin: 0; margin-inline-start: 18px; padding: 12px 0 24px; }
  /* The handle between a conversation and its thread is in the gap between their cards: unseen until the pointer finds
     it, as the list's handle is. */
  html:root #messages-screen .messages-layout > .messages-reply-pane > .messages-reply-resizer { inset-inline-start: -12px; }
  html:root #messages-screen .messages-layout > .messages-reply-pane > .messages-reply-resizer:not(:hover):not(:focus-visible) { background: none; }
}
html:root #messages-screen .messages-layout > :is(.messages-thread-pane:not(.messages-no-selection), .messages-reply-pane) {
  grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
  grid-template-rows: auto auto auto minmax(0, 1fr) auto auto auto;
  align-content: stretch;
  justify-items: stretch;
  align-items: stretch;
  isolation: isolate;
  margin: 0;
  padding: 12px 16px calc(max(var(--platform-tabs-h, 0px), var(--platform-safe-bottom, 0px)) + 12px);
  border: 0;
  border-radius: 0;
  background: transparent;
  box-shadow: none;
  -webkit-backdrop-filter: none;
  backdrop-filter: none;
}
html:root #messages-screen .messages-layout.messages-drawer > .messages-thread-pane:not(.messages-no-selection) {
  background: var(--home-wallpaper);
  box-shadow: calc(-8px * var(--rtl-sign, 1)) 0 24px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.08);
}
/* direction: physical — an iPhone Duo's column of system chrome is the screen's right side, whatever the language
   (THE SIDE STRIP): the pane's content stays clear of it, as the drawer's own rule had it. */
html[data-side-strip="right"]:root #messages-screen .messages-layout.messages-drawer > .messages-thread-pane:not(.messages-no-selection) {
  padding-right: calc(16px + var(--platform-strip-w, 0px));
}
/* direction: logical */
html.un-kb:root #messages-screen .messages-layout > :is(.messages-thread-pane:not(.messages-no-selection), .messages-reply-pane),
html.platform-kb-open:root #messages-screen .messages-layout > :is(.messages-thread-pane:not(.messages-no-selection), .messages-reply-pane) {
