/* ── PHONE AUDIT (request 7164, page by page): FIVE SMALL CONTROLS PRESSED AT 44PX ──
   Under 768px only. Nothing is drawn any larger: each control gets a tap box beyond its own shape.
   CHALLENGES' TABS (30px in a 34px track). The strip scrolls sideways, so it clips what is past its padding box:
   it takes 5px more padding above and below, pulled back by its margins so nothing under it moves, and each tab's
   box reaches into that room. The track is then drawn by the strip's ::after, 5px in, where it always was, and the
   sliding pill keeps its 2px from the track's edge.
   A THREAD'S REACTIONS (32px). The chips wrap into rows 6px apart, so a box over the chip would take the next
   row's taps. It sits under every chip of the row instead (z-index -1 in the row's own stacking context, as the
   cards' attribute chips do): a chip's own shape always wins, and the box answers only in the gaps around it.
   THE WORKSHOP'S HEAD LINKS (Open the board, a week's list, Earlier weeks: 32px). 6px more above and below, inside
   the card's own padding and the 12px over what follows.
   ALL ITEMS. A card's menu button is 28px: 8px of reach on every side, which stops at the card's edge. Its category
   chip is 22px and opens the category vote: its box, under the chip's words, is 44px tall. A chip that is only a
   label is a span and gets nothing. */
@media (max-width: 767.98px) {
  html:root #leaderboard-screen #standings-tabs.one-seg { padding-block: 7px; margin-block: -5px 7px; background: none; }
  html:root #leaderboard-screen #standings-tabs.one-seg::after { content: ""; position: absolute; z-index: -1; inset: 5px 0; border-radius: 9999px; background: var(--one-seg-track); }
  html:root #leaderboard-screen #standings-tabs.one-seg[style*="--one-seg-i"]::before { top: 7px; bottom: 7px; }
  html:root #leaderboard-screen #standings-tabs.one-seg > button::after { content: ""; position: absolute; inset: -7px 0; }
  html:root .messages-reactions { isolation: isolate; }
  html:root .messages-reactions button { position: relative; }
  html:root .messages-reactions button::after { content: ""; position: absolute; z-index: -1; inset-inline: 0; top: 50%; height: 44px; transform: translateY(-50%); }
  html:root #dev-workshop .dev-ws-front-go { position: relative; }
  html:root #dev-workshop .dev-ws-front-go::after { content: ""; position: absolute; inset-inline: 0; top: 50%; height: 44px; transform: translateY(-50%); }
  html:root #dev-workshop .dev-ws[data-ws-tab="all"] #dev-kanban .dev-ws-wrow-menu > .dev-card-menu-btn { position: relative; }
  html:root #dev-workshop .dev-ws[data-ws-tab="all"] #dev-kanban .dev-ws-wrow-menu > .dev-card-menu-btn::after { content: ""; position: absolute; inset: -8px; }
  html:root #dev-workshop .dev-ws[data-ws-tab="all"] #dev-kanban .dev-ws-wrow-status > button.attr-chip { position: relative; }
  html:root #dev-workshop .dev-ws[data-ws-tab="all"] #dev-kanban .dev-ws-wrow-status > button.attr-chip::after { content: ""; position: absolute; z-index: -1; inset-inline: 0; top: 50%; height: 44px; transform: translateY(-50%); }
}

/* ── PHONE AUDIT (request 7164, points 2 and 5): A FINGER'S REACH AND 16PX BOXES ──
   Under 768px only, in the standard look; nothing here is read on a desktop.
   TAP AREAS. The bar's own controls (Back, the bell, the Homeroom menu) carry .un-touch-target, whose ::after is a
   44px box, and the bar's 14px gap keeps the bell's box off the menu's, so they needed nothing. A conversation's
   discs (its members and its actions, and a reply thread's back and close) moved onto its title card with One look,
   where they are 34px with no box beyond the disc: each gets 5px of reach on every side, 44px in all. The card's gap
   is 12px, so two boxes stop 2px short of each other and neither takes its neighbour's taps.
   TEXT BOXES. iOS zooms the page when a box under 16px takes the cursor. Home's, Communities' and Messages' search
   were made 16px by One look; these are the ones left: the notifications search (14px), every field of Settings
   (its search and the profile card's fields 15px, the rest 14px), the profile card on You, and the board's filter
   (15px). max(1rem, 16px): the size follows Settings' Text size upward and never drops under what iOS asks for. */
@media (max-width: 767.98px) {
  html:root #messages-screen .messages-thread-header .messages-thread-action { position: relative; }
  html:root #messages-screen .messages-thread-header .messages-thread-action::after { content: ''; position: absolute; inset: -5px; }
  html:root #notifications-search-input,
  html:root #settings-screen :is(input:not([type="checkbox"], [type="radio"], [type="file"], [type="range"], [type="color"], [type="hidden"]), textarea),
  html:root :is(#profile-root, #settings-root) .profile-details-card .profile-details-input,
  html:root #dev-workshop .dev-ws[data-ws-tab="all"] #dev-kanban-search,
  html:root #dev-kanban-search { font-size: max(1rem, 16px); }
}

